    <selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Biologis Adept" hidden="false" id="05e2-aef9-5183-347a">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="5" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="21a1-84d0-453e-1b62" includeChildSelections="true"/>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9c63-e4ec-6446-38b6"/>
      </constraints>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Biologis Adept" id="de38-7b58-723a-c11c" hidden="false" type="profile" targetId="2156-be6d-b930-9caf"/>
        <infoLink name="Laspistol" id="08f1-a742-3b37-cf75" hidden="false" type="profile" targetId="95a9-d270-d218-1772"/>
        <infoLink name="Close Combat Weapon" id="3fe4-9b8f-edf4-f075" hidden="false" type="profile" targetId="46d5-85f2-d932-f0a2"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Narthecium" id="d8ef-5817-2503-f1e4" hidden="false">
          <description>The Narthecium allows the medic to ignore the first failed saving throw each turn in the unit containing the Apothecary. This may not be used on any model who suffered &apos;Instant Death&apos; or hit by a weapon that allows no saves. It cannot be used if the Apothecary is in base to base contact with an enemy model.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Sample Collectors" id="4b3a-4191-2a94-0757" hidden="false">
          <description>The adepts of the Adeptus Mechanicus‘ Divisio Biologis
are on the constant search for foreign bio-samples and will take any chance to collect new ones. A unit containing a Biologis Adept must pass a Leadership test in order to pursue a foe defeated in close combat or make a sweeping advance. If the test is failed the unit must consolidate. If the enemy were Xenos then no Leadership test is taken, and the unit must consolidate.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <entryLinks>
